    "http://cityvisionuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/dVje4t4mDq/Vice-President-Of-Partner-Care": {
      "title": "Before you Apply",
      "description": "Vice President of Partner Care - City Vision University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Before you Apply Visit our Adjunct Faculty Page to review pay and expectations for adjunct faculty. Visit our Mission, Vision and Values page to assess whether there might be a fit. Vice President of Partner Care Remote Part Time Executive Share The Vice President position reports to the Senior Vice President of Partner Care (primary) and the President (secondarily). The position is part-time (starting at 10-20 hours) and is a work-from-home position anywhere in the United States. Duties include: New Partnership Development Initiate Conversation. Contact leadership of rescue missions and other Christian ministries that serve the poor to set up initial meetings. Relationship Building. Continue to develop relationships with rescue missions and other Christian ministries that have expressed interest until they either send us students or tell us they are not interested. Develop & Deepen Existing Partnerships Deepen Relationships. Foster relationships to grow existing partnerships through regular meetings to increase student referrals to City Vision. Creative Solutions. Work with CVU academic leadership to develop creative solutions to help address the overall educational and training needs of partners, staff and students to increase their ability to outsource to CVU. Conferences and Events Attend conferences, workshops and events to set up meetings at the conference and following the conference. General Attend regular staff meetings & supervision meetings including an annual in-person staff gathering. Participate and lead staff chapel and prayer on Zoom. Assist in areas as needed by mutual agreement. Required: Individuals must have at least an accredited Bachelor's degree Previous work experience with Gospel Rescue Missions, Salvation Army, Adult & Teen Challenge, YWAM or similar ministry Have a demonstrated commitment to our Christian mission, vision and values focused on serving those who are poor and addicted Strong relationship-building, communication, and presentation skills Very strong technical expertise is required (extensive experience or training with Customer Relationship Management Database, Google Docs, Google Spreadsheets, Microsoft Word, Excel Spreadsheets and Windows). Comfortable initiating cold outreach and following up persistently and professionally U.S. citizen or lawful permanent resident alien with valid work authorization. This position is classified as a Ministerial role, as it involves the distinct religious functions of: 1) supporting the spiritual needs of partner ministries and students and 2) leading the staff in corporate worship and prayer. Desired Experience in nonprofit Development, Fundraising, or Business Development Proven ability to build trust-based relationships with senior leaders (Executive Directors, CEOs, Pastors, Program Directors) Strategic thinker with the ability to create and implement partnership solutions Demonstrated success in cultivating partnerships from initial contact through long-term engagement Compensation $35/hour Free tuition in City Vision University (undergraduate or graduate) Work from home (anywhere in the United States) ADA Requirements: Physical, Mental, and Environmental Demands 1. Physical & Sensory Demands Stationary & Digital Work: Must remain stationary (75-90% of time) to operate a computer, keyboard, and mouse. Requires repetitive hand/finger motion for extensive data entry and navigating multiple software systems. Visual & Auditory: Requires close visual acuity to analyze financial data and detect minute errors in regulations. Must clearly communicate complex instructions via video conferencing and phone. 2. Mental & Cognitive Demands Agility & Self-Regulation: Requires adaptability to fluctuating priorities in a fast-paced environment. Must self-manage time and focus effectively without direct supervision. Spiritual Leadership: Must possess the spiritual maturity and cognitive focus to align with the Christian values of partners as well as lead staff in prayer and chapel services, requiring the ability to discern and serve spiritual needs. 3. Emotional Demands Relational Complexity and Resilience : Must demonstrate high emotional intelligence to navigate complex partner dynamics, rejection (when partners are \"not interested\"), and strategic relationship deepening. Resilience & Empathy: On occasion will interact with at-risk populations in crisis. Must maintain professional composure and empathy while enforcing policies. 4. Work Environment Remote Compliance: 100% remote. Must provide a private, quiet workspace free of distractions to ensure FERPA compliance. Tech Proficiency: Requires reliable internet and fluency in digital workflows (Zoom, Google Workspace, SIS, CRM). About City Vision University City Vision University is an online-only, Christian institution with the goal of providing radically affordable education to those serving poor and addicted individuals. We currently offer Certificates, Bachelor's, Associate's and Master's in Addiction Counseling Nonprofit Management, Business and Ministry and a Doctorate in Organizational Leadership and Innovation. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Are you a Christian actively attending a church? * -- No answer -- Yes No Are able to support City Vision's statement of faith? See: https://goo.gl/sqasUx and our mission as listed at: http://www.cityvision.edu/about? * -- No answer -- Yes No Do you have previous work experience with Gospel Rescue Missions, Salvation Army, Adult and Teen Challenge or similar ministry serving those recovering from homelessness, addiction and poverty? * -- No answer -- Yes No Do you meet ALL the following required criteria for this position (listed below)? • Individuals must have at least an accredited Bachelor's degree • Strong relationship-building, communication, and presentation skills • Very strong technical expertise is required (extensive experience or training with Customer Relationship Management Database, Google Docs, Google Spreadsheets, Microsoft Word, Excel Spreadsheets and Windows). • Comfortable initiating cold outreach and following up persistently and professionally • U.S. citizen or lawful permanent resident alien with valid work authorization. * -- No answer -- Yes No Mission Alignment Please read our mission statement and history at http://www.cityvision.edu/about. Please describe how your passion and life calling aligns with our mission and focus on educating Christians that serve the poor and addicted? Are there aspects of your background that give you a particular passion for serving this audience? What experience do you have serving this audience? * Previous Experience with City Vision Ministry Partners Over 80% of our students come from City Vision Ministry Partners such as Gospel Rescue Missions, Salvation Army, Adult and Teen Challenge or similar ministries. Describe your previous work experience with Gospel Rescue Missions, Salvation Army, Adult and Teen Challenge or similar ministry serving those recovering from homelessness, addiction and poverty. * Testimony/Spiritual Journey As a Christian University, the vibrancy of the faith and spiritual life of our staff is important. Briefly share your testimony and spiritual journey. What church do you attend and what is your current church involvement? * Previous Related Experience The core competencies for this position are very similar to those in nonprofit development/fundraising, business development and/or sales. Describe your experience in these domains * General Fit Why does this position make sense for you based on your current needs and life stage? Why might you want to take this position as compared to other positions you might be considering? * Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
    },
    "https://info.jazzhr.com/job-seekers.html": {
      "title": "Trying to apply for a job?",
      "description": "For Job Seekers | JazzHR Sign In Products Compare Resources Company Request Demo Pricing Trying to apply for a job? Please read before you proceed JazzHR is an applicant tracking system (ATS) – software that businesses use to organize their hiring process and host their career pages. JazzHR is not a job board and, unfortunately, cannot help you get a job. Please navigate back to the website where you originally tried to apply for a job and try again. If you end up back here, please reach out to the organization you’re interested in working for directly. If you are looking for a job currently, most of our customers post their open roles on all major job boards like Indeed, LinkedIn, ZipRecruiter, and more. Please go directly to those sites to search for additional open roles. (And best of luck!) If you are a business looking to evaluate recruiting software for your hiring needs, please navigate to our main website to schedule time with one of our solutions consultants. What is an applicant tracking system (ATS)? Many companies that do any kind of hiring tend to use software like JazzHR to automate the recruiting process. Read up on what an applicant tracking system is. Make sure your resume is ATS-friendly Now that you know what an ATS is, check out our blog for formatting tips and tricks to help make your application stand out. 20 Interview Tips to Make a Great Impression Ready to nail that interview? Make sure you read up on Indeed’s latest article which outlines 20 ways to make a great impression during your interviews. Looking for additional job seeker resources? Check out Indeed’s Career Guide center. Go to Indeed Products JazzHR: Foundational Hiring Lever: Scalable Hiring Jobvite: Sophisticated Hiring Applicant Tracking Candidate Texting Explore Request a Demo Pricing Events Webinars Blog Resources Marketplace Compare & Choose JazzHR vs. Greenhouse JazzHR vs. Workable Customer Stories Company About Employ Careers Contact Us Press & Media Support Help Center Employ HireEd Academy FAQ Integrations Security Privacy Policy Terms of Service Connect with Us LinkedIn © 2026 Employ Inc. All rights reserved."
    }
